        fixedContent: "[SIL_DOCUMENT_CONTROL - Document Control and SIL Mode]\nThis SIL Support and Implementation Plan defines the participant Supported Independent Living service-delivery arrangement and how that arrangement is operationally implemented. Controlled modes are SIL_ONBOARDING, SIL_IMPLEMENTATION, SIL_PERIODIC_REVIEW and SIL_SUPPORT_MODEL_CHANGE.\n\n[PURPOSE_SCOPE_BOUNDARY - Purpose, Scope and Professional Boundary]\nThe plan operationalises approved/current SIL supports. It may define support model, ratios, time bands, individual/shared support, implementation duties, readiness, handoffs, monitoring, variance and escalation. It must not decide funding, invent ratios, construct rosters, create clinical/BSP/RP instructions, make tenancy/housing/SDA decisions, or investigate incidents.\n\n[EVIDENCE_REVIEWED - Evidence Reviewed and Currentness]\nCurrent evidence controls the SIL plan. Historical support arrangements do not remain active unless current approved evidence establishes them.",
