        fixedContent: "[GOVERNANCE_MONITORING - SIL Governance and Monitoring]\nThe SIL model must define how implementation will be monitored and what triggers early review.\n\n[GOVERNANCE_MONITORING_DOMAINS - Governance Monitoring Domains]\nMinimum domains include PARTICIPANT_CHOICE_AND_CONTROL, SAFEGUARDING, PRACTICE_GOVERNANCE, STAFF_COMPETENCY, ROSTER_SKILL_MIX, TENANCY_SUPPORT_SEPARATION, INCIDENT_COMPLAINT_TRENDS, PARTICIPANT_FEEDBACK and SUPPORT_MODEL_IMPLEMENTATION.",
        fields: ["[GOVERNANCE_MONITORING - SIL Governance and Monitoring]", "Table: monitoring area | method/evidence | responsible owner | frequency | trigger for early review | action if gap identified. Sources may include shift notes, handovers, house checks, supervision, incidents, complaints, participant feedback, house meetings, competency review, roster skill mix, safeguarding review, RP monitoring, Care Plan review, governance meetings and corrective-action register.", "[GOVERNANCE_MONITORING_DOMAINS - Governance Monitoring Domains]", "Table: domain | applies? | monitoring source | owner | frequency/source | issue identified | action required | status."],
