        title: "Implementation Variance, Review and Change Control",
        existingProse: "[IMPLEMENTATION_VARIANCE - Implementation Variance]\nDescription: Identifies where actual implementation is not aligned with approved/current model. Instructions: Treat variance as an operational review issue and route specialist matters.\n\n[REVIEW_CHANGE_CONTROL - Review, Change and Model Update Triggers]\nDescription: Defines when the SIL arrangement must be reviewed or changed. Instructions: Do not independently approve the underlying funding/clinical basis for a change.",
        fixedContent: "[IMPLEMENTATION_VARIANCE - Implementation Variance]\nImplementation variance must be identified, classified, assigned and monitored until resolved or escalated.\n\n[REVIEW_CHANGE_CONTROL - Review, Change and Model Update Triggers]\nSIL review/change must be triggered where evidence shows material change, gap, risk, variance, participant concern or professional authority issue.",
        fields: ["[IMPLEMENTATION_VARIANCE - Implementation Variance]", "Table: variance type | approved/current requirement | actual implementation | evidence | impact | immediate action | owner | escalation required | status. Variance may include ratio not delivered, competency unavailable, required plan unavailable, support not delivered, shared support not implemented as approved, overnight arrangement inconsistent, routine/support requirement not followed, BSP/RP/medication/mealtime gap, documentation gap, environment incompatibility or other SIL implementation variance.", "[REVIEW_CHANGE_CONTROL - Review, Change and Model Update Triggers]", "Table: trigger | evidence | required review/change | owner | external authority required | interim action | due date | status. Triggers include support model change, participant need change, ratio/hours issue, funding/support evidence change, service environment change, staffing/competency gap, incident/complaint trend, BSP/RP/clinical/medication/mealtime update or participant/representative concern."],
